From d5c3e61f792074d9f480f4fa99a35940415da0b8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vishnu Ramadas <vramadas@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 16:52:54 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] plugins/amdgpu: add amdgpu_plugin_gem5 for restores in gem5

Build a second amdgpu plugin, gem5/amdgpu_plugin_gem5.so
(-DAMDGPU_PLUGIN_GEM5), for restoring MI300X checkpoints inside a gem5
GPU full-system guest. The stock amdgpu_plugin.so is built from the same
sources without it and behaves as upstream. CRIU loads every plugin in
its -L directory, so the gem5 plugin is built and installed in its own
gem5/ subdirectory: -L plugins/amdgpu selects the stock plugin,
-L plugins/amdgpu/gem5 the gem5 one.

The gem5 plugin differs from the stock one in three ways:

- Restore onto a subset of the checkpointed GPUs (on by default,
  KFD_RESTORE_GPU_SUBSET=0 turns it off). The ROCm runtime opens every
  visible GPU, so a process that computes on one GPU of an 8-GPU node is
  checkpointed with a KFD process device for every GPU, and a stock
  restore needs all of them. GPUs that hold no state besides their
  MMIO-remap page are left out: their device entries and MMIO-remap BOs
  are not restored, they are removed from BO mapped_gpuids and SVM
  attributes in the KFD private data (KFD_CRIU_PRIV_VERSION 1 only), and
  their render-node fds and MMIO-page CPU mappings go to the kept GPU.
  Image files are not modified; everything is rewritten in memory.

- io_links_count of a checkpointed GPU counts only links whose peer is in
  the checkpoint. The stored value is the raw sysfs count, which also
  counts links to nodes the dump could not see (a device cgroup exposing
  one CPX partition stores 15 links but serializes 1) and links to GPUs
  left out above; neither is restored, so neither takes part in the
  topology match.

- SDMA COPY_LINEAR count is bytes - 1 on AMDGPU_FAMILY_AI and newer, as
  the kernel's sdma_v4+ emit_copy_buffer writes it. The plugin writes the
  byte count, which copies one byte past the end of both buffers; gem5's
  SDMA model executes exactly that and corrupts the neighbouring data.
  The stock plugin keeps upstream's count.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
